WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-ES

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.560
Hello, welcome back
to Lam Rim.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:12.040
We're starting
episode number 9.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.960
I like to call it
"A Visit to the Center of the Sun".  We've been

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.520
talking

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.000
about something that's big enough


00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.760
and powerful enough,

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:29.920
it's like a nuclear bomb used
to clean ketchup off your blouse or something.

00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:37.040
And I'm not exaggerating.
I want you to think like this.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.520
Imagine...

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.600
So today in the United States, it's
Independence Day.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:44.600
I'm speaking on
Independence Day,

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.520
and many times we go on
a picnic with our family.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:54.160
It's the middle of summer.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.040
And American children will eat
hot dogs or hamburgers

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.080
and put a lot of ketchup on them,

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:05.120
and a tiny, tiny squirt of ketchup will
fall here.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.200
Imagine that to clean it,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.600
the mother sends the shirt
or blouse into the center of the sun...

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.520
[inaudible]

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.120
...to clean a little bit
of ketchup, red ketchup.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.360
I know it sounds like
a strange image,

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:32.080
but I'd like you to try to think about it.  I would like you to
try to think about that.  I do

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.280
n't know what to compare it to.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:40.120
Yes, I don't know.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:43.480
Just put a small thing
in the center of the sun, okay?

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:47.560
So let's visit the center of the sun
today.

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:51.240
And I'm happy to announce

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:56.400
that we've just reached the third
and final section of the Lam Rim.

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.080
The steps on the path
to enlightenment.

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:03.240
From this moment on
we are about to move on

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.040
to the activities of a bodhisattva.

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:13.000
We are about to start thinking
and acting like a bodhisattva,

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:17.200
who is the person of greatest ability.
(KYES BU CHEN PO)

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.240
Which means a person
of great ability.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:25.640
Those of you, especially those
of you who have followed this Lam Rim

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:27.960
for the past ten years,

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:31.040
should be super happy
that we have survived

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.160
and that I have survived to reach
the final part.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:40.080
We're in the final part.
It's the last third.  Now...

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:45.360
those mathematicians among you
should be thinking: "Okay, Geshela,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:49.280
"you just said we have 25%
to go.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.360
So why is that
the last third?"

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:59.160
And the answer is that
Pabongka Rinpoche's treatise

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:04.200
on the last two days of Lam Rim
is too short.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:10.480
His presentation of meditation
and his presentation of seeing emptiness,

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:16.280
the last two of the six perfections,
isn't very long.

00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.120
And I don't know what happened. I
mean, sometimes it's... it's

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:21.120
like...

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:24.600
if the sponsor came up to him and said,
"We're going to run out of food in two days."  "It's

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.760
almost over."

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.720
It's possible...

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:32.160
maybe it's a mystical message from Tara,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:38.280
or maybe, I don't know, maybe he had another appointment
in another city.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:42.120
But if you ask me,

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.480
Pabongka Rinpoche made the last two parts
shorter

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:52.040
because Je Tsongkhapa had already covered them
in his great Lam Rim,

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.160
"The Great Book on the Steps on the Path
to Enlightenment," the Lam Rim Chenmo.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.920
Tsongkhapa did such a great job

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:02.600
that I think I can see Pabongka Rinpoche
saying,

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:08.000
"You know, guys, there's not much reason for me to
teach this part

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:14.360
because Tsongkhapa already taught it,
and he did it extraordinarily well."

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:19.840
There are many stories about Tsongkhapa
writing those last two parts,

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:22.760
and I'm so happy that we're going
to do them together.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.720
So we're going to finish this
Lam Rim series

00:04:25.720 --> 00:04:30.880
with amazing teachings on meditation
and emptiness.

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:35.000
So that's why this part

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:41.480
on the steps on the path for people
who have bodhichitta, for Bodhisattvas,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:44.880
isn't as long
as it could have been.

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.040
So here we go.
Let's...  Read the Tibetan.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:52.480
(GSUM PA SKYES BU CHEN PO'I LAM GYI RIM
PAR BLO SBYANG BA LA)

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.680
Let us train our hearts

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:57.040
in the steps on the path

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:59.280
for people of great ability.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:01.760
People who are bodhisattvas.

00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:05.640
(THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA)

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.280
It says that we are going to cover this,
the lifestyle of a bodhisattva, we

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.080
will cover it in three different steps.

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.520
Number one.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.640
(THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO)
If you want to enter the path of the bodhisattva,

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:21.480
there is only one way
to get there.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.520
And that is by attaining
a certain state of mind.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:31.200
If you want to become enlightened, if you want to have
the opportunity to become enlightened,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.840
if you want to have the opportunity
to help the world, there is

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:37.400
only one way.
You have to attain bodhichitta.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.040
You have to get this desire

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:46.000
to attain enlightenment
so that you can help countless beings.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.480
Now, I want to talk about countless.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:54.480
The  Bodhichitta is directed
toward countless living beings. It's

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.760
not directed toward every person in your city
or every person in your country

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.480
or every person
on this planet.

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.480
Forget that;

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:07.760
if we want to send the virus to the center of the sun,
if we want to visit the center of the sun,

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:11.120
forget this idea

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.000
that we're working
for every person on this planet. We're

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.080
not.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:19.160
Forget this idea that we're trying
to help

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.680
every fish and every bird
and every

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.040
animal that walks
on land—

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.080
we're not, that's not the point.

00:06:28.560 --> 00:06:32.120
We're covering the entire universe.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:38.000
We're deciding today
that I would like to help

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:41.840
every living being in the universe.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:46.280
Every tiny virus, every bacterium.

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:49.080
Every whale.

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:52.720
Every human in the universe.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:07:00.000
So, go outside at night in Sedona,
or outside of Sedona—Rim Rock is better—

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.240
and look at the stars and try to imagine.

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:13.960
Then, first, you can't practice
the lifestyle of a bodhisattva

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:22.800
if you don't expand your mind toward that...
toward that goal.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:29.880
And if you really experience it,
what  It takes some practice.

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:32.440
If you truly send your mind,

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:37.920
if you are truly able to attain
bodhichitta,

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:42.480
then the things you have to do
in this world are nothing. There is

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:46.520
nothing.
It is insignificant.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:51.240
Helping all the people
in this world is nothing. It

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:53.640
is easy.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:59.520
(PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA) means:
I want to tell you the benefits of thinking like this.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:00.960
That is the first step.

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:03.960
(BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED PA'I TSUL)
Second step.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.760
How do you arrive at this great breakthrough?
Mental breakthrough?

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:12.920
How do you perceive the entire universe
and all beings in it?

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:17.920
And then develop love for them.
Is it possible?

00:08:17.920 --> 00:08:20.720
Is it possible?
That is the second step.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:25.400
Third step.
(SEMS BSKYED NAS SPYOD PA LA SLOB TSUL LO)

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.040
Let's learn how to act
like a bodhisattva.

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:33.000
Once you have this hope
of becoming a bodhisattva,

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:36.000
well then, practically,
what am I supposed to do?

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:43.040
How do I spend the hours of my day
if  Do I want to act like a bodhisattva?

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:45.600
What should I do?

00:08:45.680 --> 00:08:50.080
What will my agenda be?

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:53.040
Well. Here's the first one.

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:57.000
(DANG PO NI, DE LTAR SKYES BU CHUNG
'BRING GI SKABS SU)

00:08:57.000 --> 00:09:00.120
(SKABS SU NGES 'BYUNG GI BSAM
PAS KUN NAS BSLANGS)

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:04.720
So now that we've gone through the steps
on the path

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:09.640
for people of lesser
and middle ability,

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:14.880
at least you should have this feeling
that...

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.920
really, life is pain,
really, this life is a problem.

00:09:17.920 --> 00:09:21.720
The virus makes it obvious.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:24.000
But it's always been like this. There's

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.960
always been a virus
called death.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:31.760
This virus is the new one.
It's much smaller.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:35.280
But at least now we're all
thinking about it.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:38.960
(LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM LA 'BAD PAS)

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:44.040
Then, we were supposed to work
on the three extraordinary trainings.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.040
Treat other people well.

00:09:47.040 --> 00:09:49.520
Spend time in meditation.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:54.120
And then try to see that things
don't come from your own side.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:58.680
('BAD PAS RANG GCIG PUS  (THAR BA'I GO
'PHANG THOB TZAM)

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:00.960
(DANG 'KHOR BA LAS LDOG TZAM 'BYUNG)

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:04.280
You can reach nirvana by yourself

00:10:04.280 --> 00:10:08.360
and you can get out of the Wheel of Life.

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:12.320
If you practice with these attitudes, you can,
it is possible. We

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.880
already taught you this, we already finished
with that.

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.320
(DE TZAM GYIS MI CHOG)

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:19.680
But I don't want you to stop there. I do

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.200
n't want you to stop there.
I want you to... There is much more

00:10:22.200 --> 00:10:26.520
to do. There is

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:32.000
much more to do.
Don't stop there.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:35.720
(SPANG BYA THAMS CAD MA SPANGS)

00:10:36.520 --> 00:10:41.000
If you stick to what I taught you
so far, you

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:44.240
will not cleanse your heart

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.080
of all the impure things
that are there.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:51.120
(THOB BYA YON TAN THAMS CAD KYANG
YONGS SU MA RDZOGS PAS)

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:52.240
And you have not attained

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:56.080
all the higher spiritual qualities
that you could have attained.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.040
(MA RDZOGS PAS)
Therefore

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:03.720
(RANG DON DANG, GZHAN  (DON YANG NYI
TSE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG)

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:10.480
(NYI TSE BA)
There's a very discouraging word here.

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.520
There's a very sad word here.

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:17.240
It says, you can work on those paths I've
taught you so far, you can

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:21.440
work on all those meditations I've
taught you so far,

00:11:21.440 --> 00:11:26.400
but the amount of good you will do
for yourself and others

00:11:26.400 --> 00:11:30.080
is only a small amount
of what you need to do.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.960
(NYI TSE BA)
means:

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:36.680
it's only a small amount
of what you should be doing.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:42.000
And, by the way, the most common use
of that word is...

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:45.440
it's the Tibetan word for hell
on earth.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:46.880
Which is very strange.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:51.200
So there's a big hell that people
can go to.

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:56.040
But I always think of a person who had
a car accident and the car exploded

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.120
and they're engulfed in flames.

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:03.440
In the scriptures, that's called
(NYI TSI BA'I DMYAL BA),

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:09.800
a little piece of hell on this plane.
On this plane of reality.

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:13.920
And so this word (NYI TSI BA)
means just a small piece.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:19.720
And here  He says, "Do you want to help yourself
and do you want to help other people?

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.520
Everything I've taught you so far for
10 years

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.040
(NYI TSI BA)

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:26.640
is only a small fraction

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:31.280
of what you could be doing, and now
we're ready to start with the serious stuff."

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:34.520
"Well, Geshe-la,
why did we spend 10 years

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:38.080
doing the (NYI TSI BA),
the little things?

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:40.640
Why didn't we just go
to the higher things?"

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:45.760
Because small things are a ladder
that helps you reach higher things.  You ca

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:51.880
n't reach the highest things
unless you do the other two parts.

00:12:51.880 --> 00:12:54.880
Unless you practice all the steps
of Lam Rim

00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:57.040
in their correct order,

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.880
you will never reach the
bodhisattva part.

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:03.400
So, you can't say you don't
want them.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:07.440
Part of the bodhisattva lifestyle

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:11.480
is mastering the lower path
that helped you get there.

00:13:11.480 --> 00:13:16.640
And you never reject them.  You
simply grow from them.

00:13:16.640 --> 00:13:23.480
(MI 'BYUNG ZHING SLAR THEG CHEN
LA GZHI NAS 'JUG DGOS LA)

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:29.240
This is an idea in Buddhism,

00:13:29.960 --> 00:13:31.360
that as soon as you are ready,

00:13:31.360 --> 00:13:34.400
and as soon as you have
the preparation,

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:39.240
you should jump straight into the
bodhisattva lifestyle, because...

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:43.600
if you don't, you're going to have to do it again
anyway.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:46.520
So, sooner or later
you have to get here.

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:51.360
Maybe this lifetime will take you.
Perhaps it will be later in this life.

00:13:51.360 --> 00:13:55.720
People approach me from time to time
and say,

00:13:55.720 --> 00:13:59.480
"I'm going to take a break
from this Dharma.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:03.440
I feel like I need to take
a break."

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:06.720
"There are other things I
have to do now.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:13.840
"I have a big project at work,"
or: "I have family things going on

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:16.640
and I need to take a break."

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:21.920
I said that to one of my teachers in India, I
remember.

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:26.480
45 years ago.

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:30.960
And I said, "I need to take a break."
And he looked at me and said,

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.360
"Yes, that's fine."  But you will return.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:38.160
"You will return because there is nowhere else to
go.

00:14:38.160 --> 00:14:39.600
You will return."

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:46.200
You will return to this because you need to return to this.
Life will bring you back here.

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:49.960
Because that's how life is.
You need the Lam Rim.

00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:54.200
Life will always bring you back to the Lam Rim, unless you die.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:58.760
And it will still bring you back
to it later.

00:14:58.760 --> 00:15:03.720
(SLAR) means you have to come back again.
(SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS)

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:08.360
(GZHI NAS) means you're going to waste a lot of time
if you have to go back to it.

00:15:08.360 --> 00:15:13.760
It's better to do it now
rather than come back to it later.

00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.360
The next image here

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:26.080
is a little bit of something I want to do with you
in this episode, episode nine.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:30.240
I call it "A Visit to the Center of the Sun."
So in this image, I

00:15:30.240 --> 00:15:34.640
tried to find an image...

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:41.840
that's close to what it feels like to have
bodhichitta.

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.120
So this image looks a little...

00:15:44.120 --> 00:15:48.040
we were saying, Seiji, Tim, and I,
that it's a little "new agey."

00:15:48.040 --> 00:15:52.280
It looks like it was painted in Sedona, Arizona.

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:57.200
It feels a little new age,
but let me say something.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:00.480
If
you ever get bodhichitta,

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:02.000
it will feel...

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:05.120
this image is very  Close.
This image is kind of close.

00:16:05.120 --> 00:16:11.160
Can you put it down?
Just for a minute?

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:17.440
This image isn't crazy,
and it's not some kind of hippie thing.

00:16:17.440 --> 00:16:23.960
When you reach bodhichitta, real bodhichitta,
it feels very much like this.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:29.120
So maybe you'd like to make a copy of this image. We
already paid for it.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:33.240
So you could use it at home.
You could have it at home.

00:16:33.240 --> 00:16:39.880
You could have an image like that.
Maybe put it as your phone's screensaver.

00:16:39.880 --> 00:16:44.480
It's pretty close to what it feels like to
get bodhichitta.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:48.040
So I'd like to take you
on a little trip,

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:52.160
just for fun,
maybe five minutes.

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:57.360
